  "body": "Part of #1442 (lathe chuck fixtures). The first slice (PR for issue/1442-lathe-chuck-fixtures) generates 3-jaw, 4-jaw and collet chucks as built-in accessories, placed by pose or fitted to round stock over MCP (`add_accessory` `fit_to_stock`), read by the lathe holder law and the post gate. Left for this issue:\n\n- **UI fit to the stock:** the \"Add accessory…\" dialog lists the three chucks and places them by pose; it has no \"Fit to the stock\" toggle for a chuck (the `OnStock` placement exists in the command). Add it, with structural-test assertions (no snapshot PNGs).\n- **Viewport look verified** in the running app, with before/after screenshots for the PR.\n- **Inside (ID) grip** and **stepped jaws** (a step height/depth the work sits on).\n- **Independent 4-jaw offsets** (each jaw's own radial position, off-centre work).\n- **Chuck rpm limit** feeding the workholding/spindle-speed checks (see #1031 if still open).\n- **Chuck on a rotary axis of a milling setup** (4th-axis chuck; frame along the rotary axis rather than +z).\n- **camcraft-mcp skill row** for the chuck kinds and `fit_to_stock`.\n\nDone means: the dialog offers \"Fit to the stock\" for chucks (pinned by a UI test), inside grip and stepped jaws are chuck figures with validation by name and envelope tests, and the camcraft-mcp skill lists the chuck kinds.\n",
